<%# Every answer the impression frame can give (story 0033, redesigned
    2026-09-01). Locals: painting, pick (the DailyPick this painting is
    scheduled on, or nil), impression (the reader's own line, or nil),
    archived: (the `view=answer` request, front_door's ONE opposite —
    read-only, never a composer, never a hint), editing: (`?edit=1`, tap
    own comment for the day), answered: (today, signed in, has a line, not
    editing — computed once in the controller, not re-derived here).

    The frame id matches the caller's inert or eager frame in every state —
    an unmatched response is Turbo's "Content missing" painted over the
    calm page (eng A1). Privacy order: the comment only for its author; the
    composer only for a signed-in reader on today's pick, still looking;
    the sign-in hint (plain text, no link, no form, no cookie — the wall's
    401 frame carries a link and must never appear here) for everyone else;
    and on `archived`, silence for anyone without a line — a hint on a page
    that never offered writing would be a nag.

    The prompt is the one thing the composer and the hint states share —
    hoisted into one render site below rather than duplicated across both,
    since it renders identically either way. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "impression_#{painting.id}" do %>
  <% if archived %>
    <% if impression %>
      <%= render layout: "impressions/row" do %>
        <p class="cmt__body cmt__body--mine">
          <span class="cmt__who">You</span>&ensp;<%= impression.body %>
        </p>
        <p class="cmt__meta"><%= render "impressions/time", impression: impression %></p>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif answered %>
    <%# Today's pick, answered: the comment, tap to edit (eng OV1 — the
        day-end ink boundary, not a blur or a reveal). No submit button,
        no Turbo on the composer form below: autosave_controller — mounted
        once, on the persistent frame in `daily/_day.html.erb` — owns
        every write and every transition between this state and that
        one. %>
    <%= render layout: "impressions/row" do %>
      <button type="button" class="cmt__body cmt__body--mine cmt__edit"
              data-action="click->autosave#edit"
              aria-label="Edit your answer to <%= painting.title %>">
        <span class="cmt__who">You</span>&ensp;<%= impression.body %>
      </button>
      <p class="cmt__meta"><%= render "impressions/time", impression: impression %></p>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%= render layout: "impressions/row" do %>
      <p class="sit__prompt" id="sit-prompt"><%= pick&.sit_prompt %></p>
      <% if current_user %>
        <%# The composer. The day's prompt above is the field's visible
            label (aria-labelledby); the placeholder is a hint beside it,
            never the label itself. %>
        <%= form_with url: impression_path(painting), method: :post,
              class: "sit__form", data: { turbo: false } do %>
          <input type="text" name="body" class="sit__input"
                 maxlength="280" value="<%= impression&.body %>"
                 aria-labelledby="sit-prompt"
                 placeholder="Write here — even one line will do."
                 data-autosave-target="input"
                 data-action="input->autosave#changed keydown->autosave#keydown blur->autosave#blurred">
          <p class="sit__saved" aria-live="polite" data-autosave-target="status"
             data-saved-copy="Saved"></p>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%# A stranger or a registered device — the branch is current_user,
            never identified? (eng OV2/0032's own A1): a device passes the
            wall, and the field never renders for one, so it gets the same
            looking scaffold as everyone with no account. %>
        <p class="sit__hint">Sign in to keep your answer.</p>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
